        "original_id": "eb16b8b7-dc5f-54ee-96c6-0e3e0e6bc773",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: 8 Spruce Street, Lower Manhattan, Manhattan, New York City, City Hall Park, Brooklyn Bridge\n- Buildings: Beekman Tower, New York by Gehry, World Trade Center\n- People: Frank Gehry\n- Topics: skyscrapers, building complexes\n\nFacts:\n- The original World Trade Center was a complex of seven buildings in Lower Manhattan, New York City, United States.\n- 8 Spruce Street is a 76-story skyscraper in Manhattan at 8 Spruce Street between William Street and Nassau Street in Lower Manhattan, south of City Hall Park and the Brooklyn Bridge.\n- 8 Spruce Street was originally known as Beekman Tower and is currently marketed as New York by Gehry.\n- Architect Frank Gehry designed 8 Spruce Street.",
